{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 13, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "James Carter woke up to the blaring sound of a video game’s title screen, his vision swimming into focus as the words *\"LOADING…\"* flickered across his retinas. He bolted upright, gripping the edges of his bed—only for his fingers to sink into fabric that felt like a cheap couch cushion. The walls around him pulsed with the faint glow of a pixelated sky, and when he reached for his nightstand, his hand passed through the lamp instead of touching it. A notification popped up in front of his face: *\"WARNING: REALITY DISRUPTION DETECTED. PLEASE STAND BY.\"* His pulse pounded in his ears as he noticed his reflection in a nearby window, but when he blinked, his avatar—a blocky, pixelated version of himself—didn’t blink back. Panic set in as he realized the controllers in his hands weren’t his own, but the game itself had already begun.\n\nThe first thing James did was check his inventory, fingers hovering over the virtual screen that now hovered in the air like an HUD. His stats were there—*HEALTH: 100/100, STAMINA: 80/100*—but his abilities were locked behind a door labeled *\"LEVEL UP: UNLOCK WHEN READY.\"* Outside his makeshift \"home,\" the world stretched endlessly, dotted with NPCs who stared at him with hollow, glitching eyes. A merchant nearby shouted, *\"Buy the sword, hero!\"* before dissolving into static. James took a deep breath and stepped forward—his feet sinking into a landscape that shifted beneath him like a badly rendered landscape. He had no idea how he’d ended up here, but one thing was clear: the game had rules, and if he wanted to escape, he’d have to learn them fast.", "logprobs": [{"token": "James", "logprob": -2.8621129989624023}, {"token": " Carter", "logprob": -1.0174413919448853}, {"token": " woke", "logprob": -1.4384487867355347}, {"token": " up", "logprob": -0.6899886131286621}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -1.18